title: Constitutional Reform
subtitle: A New Ruusan: entrench the Senate's safeguards in the constitution.
is-card: true
tags: senate_affairs
card-image: img/card_law.svg
view-if: constitution_timer <= 0 and chair_constitution = "rc" and cardok_constitution
on-arrival: amend_threshold = 66.7 if faith < 60; amend_threshold = 60 if faith >= 60; turn_actions += 1; constitution_timer = 3; last_card_timer = "constitution"
new-page: true
on-display: {! SW.cardStuck(Q, this); !}

= Constitutional Reform

Constitutional amendments need **two-thirds** of the Senate (three-fifths if faith in the Republic is 60 or more, because the member worlds can be asked to ratify them), and delegations on Palpatine's payroll vote against anything that limits the Chancellor's power. Each attempt costs 1 political capital, whether it passes or not. Senate resolve ([+ senate_resolve : resolve +]) and faith in the Republic ([+ faith : faith +]) make reform easier.

- @sunset: Sunset clauses on all emergency powers.
- @terms: Entrench the Chancellor's term limit.
- @vonc: A constructive vote of no confidence.
- @rim: Constitutional seats for the Outer Rim.
- @powers_review: The Powers Review Act.
- @speaker: An independent Speaker of the Senate.
- @groundwork: Build support for a future amendment.
- @easy_discard
- @set_aside

@sunset
view-if: not emergency_sunset
subtitle: Emergency powers will lapse unless the Senate renews them every year.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.constitution_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.55, rim: 0.65, sec: 0.25, ind: 0.6, pal: 0.15 + (Q.emergency_powers < 1 ? 0.25 : 0), cis: 0.6}, true);
Q.cr_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', 'constitution']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Sunset Amendment', Q.cr_vote, Q.amend_threshold);
if (Q.cr_vote >= Q.amend_threshold) { Q.emergency_sunset = 1; Q.faith += 1; this.achieve('sunset'); }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if emergency_sunset : From now on, every emergency power granted to the Chancellor expires after a year unless the Senate votes to renew it. ?][? if not emergency_sunset : The amendment fails. ?]

@terms
view-if: not term_limits_protected
subtitle: No Chancellor's term could ever be extended, emergency or not.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.65, guild: 0.5, rim: 0.65, sec: 0.35, ind: 0.6, pal: (Q.pal_chancellor ? 0.05 : 0.4), cis: 0.6}, true);
Q.cr_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', 'constitution']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Term Limits Amendment', Q.cr_vote, Q.amend_threshold);
if (Q.cr_vote >= Q.amend_threshold) { Q.term_limits_protected = 1; Q.faith += 1; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if term_limits_protected : The Chancellor's two-term limit is now beyond the reach of any emergency. ?][? if not term_limits_protected : The amendment fails. ?]

@vonc
view-if: not constructive_vonc
subtitle: A government can only be brought down if the Senate agrees on its replacement. More stable coalitions.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.7, guild: 0.45, rim: 0.45, sec: 0.5, ind: 0.55, pal: 0.3, cis: 0.3}, true);
Q.cr_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', 'constitution']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Constructive No-Confidence Amendment', Q.cr_vote, Q.amend_threshold);
if (Q.cr_vote >= Q.amend_threshold) { Q.constructive_vonc = 1; Q.coalition_dissent -= 1; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if constructive_vonc : Governments will no longer fall to paralysis and procedural ambush. Nobody can do to a future Chancellor what was done to Valorum. ?][? if not constructive_vonc : The amendment fails. ?]

@rim
view-if: not rim_enfranchised and rim_relief_act
subtitle: Permanent constitutional seats for the Outer Rim.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.constitution_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.35, guild: 0.25, rim: 0.95, sec: 0.2, ind: 0.6, pal: 0.35, cis: 0.75}, true);
Q.cr_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['rim', 'representation']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Rim Representation Amendment', Q.cr_vote, Q.amend_threshold);
if (Q.cr_vote >= Q.amend_threshold) { Q.rim_enfranchised = 1; Q.outer_sep -= 10; Q.midrim_sep -= 6; Q.rim_relation += 10; Q.outer_rc += 3; this.achieve('enfranchised'); }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if rim_enfranchised : The Outer Rim gains permanent seats and a constitutional voice. ?][? if not rim_enfranchised : The amendment fails. ?]


@powers_review
view-if: emergency_sunset and not powers_review
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Senate reviews the emergency powers every year, and takes them back.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.constitution_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.6, guild: 0.5, rim: 0.65, sec: 0.2, ind: 0.65, pal: 0.1, cis: 0.6}, true);
Q.pr_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', '-powers', 'constitution']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Powers Review Amendment', Q.pr_vote, Q.amend_threshold);
if (Q.pr_vote >= Q.amend_threshold) { Q.powers_review = 1; Q.faith += 1; Q.senate_resolve += 0.5; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if powers_review : The amendment passes. Every year a joint committee of the Senate will review each emergency power the Chancellery holds, and the Senate will vote to take one back. The war powers will no longer simply accumulate. ?][? if not powers_review : The amendment falls short. The Chancellery's powers will outlast the emergencies that justified them. ?]

@speaker
view-if: constructive_vonc and not independent_speaker
subtitle: −1 political capital. The Chancellor would no longer preside over the Senate, or decide what it debates.
choose-if: capital >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough political capital.
on-arrival: {!
Q.constitution_timer = 1;
Q.capital -= 1;
var st = SW.stance(Q, {mod: 0.65, guild: 0.45, rim: 0.6, sec: 0.35, ind: 0.65, pal: (Q.pal_chancellor ? 0.05 : 0.3), cis: 0.55}, true);
Q.sp_vote = SW.vote(Q, st, 1, ['oversight', 'constitution']);
Q.vote_html = SW.voteBanner('Independent Speaker Amendment', Q.sp_vote, Q.amend_threshold);
if (Q.sp_vote >= Q.amend_threshold) { Q.independent_speaker = 1; Q.senate_resolve += 0.5; Q.faith += 1; }
!}

[+ vote_html +]

[? if independent_speaker : For a thousand years the Supreme Chancellor has presided over the Senate from the podium at its centre, deciding who speaks and what is debated. From now on the Senate elects its own Speaker for that, and the Chancellor sits among the senators to answer them. The Vice Chair's gavel is a ceremonial thing at last. ?][? if not independent_speaker : The amendment fails. The podium stays where it is. ?]

@groundwork
subtitle: Free. Makes future constitutional votes a little easier.
on-arrival: new_ruusan += 1; senate_resolve += 0.3

The Caucus circulates draft amendments and gathers co-sponsors.
